---
import TopicPage from '../../../../components/TopicPage.astro';
import Widget from '../../../../components/Widget.astro';

const csaCfg = {
  steps: [
    { math: '1 · Agriculture is hit and cause', note: 'The sector absorbs climate damage (heat-stressed yields, water chaos, pest range shifts) while emitting ~a quarter of greenhouse gases — the climate lesson\'s numbers. Climate-smart agriculture = produce more, on a hotter planet, with fewer emissions.' },
    { math: '2 · Adaptation on the farm', note: 'Drought-tolerant varieties (DT maize spreading across Africa — the breeding lesson\'s delivery), water harvesting and drip (the water lesson), adjusted planting dates, agroforestry\'s microclimate, index-based livestock insurance (payout by rainfall index — no claims adjusters needed).' },
    { math: '3 · Mitigation from the soil up', note: 'Soil carbon sequestration (regenerative practices — the soil lesson, with carbon payments attached), enteric-methane feed additives, rice paddy water management (methane falls when paddies drain mid-season), and fertiliser precision (N₂O — the geochemical lesson\'s greenhouse nobody quotes).' },
    { math: '4 · The carbon-market question', note: 'Soil carbon credits: real mechanism, real measurement problems (additionality, permanence, verification — the offsets critique in the environmental-economics lesson). Buyers now pay for measured outcomes, not practices claimed — the discipline tightening in real time.' },
  ],
};
---
<TopicPage slug="subjects/agriculture/expert/climate-smart-agriculture">
  <h2>The idea</h2>
  <p>
    Climate-smart agriculture is <strong>the atlas\'s three-way intersection</strong>: the
    agronomy lessons producing food, the climate lessons forcing adaptation, and the mitigation
    lesson\'s arithmetic demanding fewer emissions — all on the same hectare.
  </p>

  <Widget no="1" caption="hit-and-cause, farm adaptation, soil mitigation, carbon markets" widget="equationStep" config={csaCfg} />

  <h2>The honest frontier</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Adaptation is already happening:</strong> planting-zone maps have shifted; coffee is moving uphill; the tropics face the cruellest arithmetic (crop yields fall with each degree — the IPCC\'s graded risks, agrarian chapter).</li>
    <li><strong>Measurement is the bottleneck, not intention:</strong> remote-sensing MRV (the precision lesson\'s stack) prices soil-carbon programmes; cheap in-field sensors and satellite models are closing the verification gap that sank the first credit wave.</li>
    <li><strong>The finance flows are the frontier:</strong> climate finance for agriculture lags its emissions share; the blended-finance and resilience-bond structures (the finance lesson\'s instruments) are being pointed at smallholder adaptation now.</li>
    <li><strong>Where the ladder lands:</strong> agriculture is the one sector that must simultaneously feed more, emit less and adapt — which is why it is the atlas\'s final synthesis subject: every other ladder feeds this one.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="sources"><strong>Sources:</strong> FAO CSA sourcebook; IPCC AR6 WGII (food chapter); the climate, soil and mitigation lessons of this atlas.</p>
</TopicPage>
